/**
 * One menu place, with the `social` one drawn as icons
 *
 * An override of the CMS's `views/menu.phtml`, which renders every place as a list of labels.
 * That is right for the main menu and wrong for the row of social links in the header, where the
 * label is the *name of a site* and what belongs on the page is its mark.
 *
 * **The URL decides**, not a field on the item: a menu item that points at `github.com` gets the
 * GitHub mark. So adding one is adding an external-address menu item and nothing else, and a host
 * with no icon here falls back to its label rather than disappearing - which is what keeps this
 * from being a list somebody has to maintain in two places.
 *
 * The label survives as `aria-label` and as the `title`, so an icon that means nothing to a
 * screen reader still announces the name of the site it points at.
 *
 * Icons are Font Awesome Free (CC BY 4.0) - the same marks the original site already serves.
 */
